PREAMBLE

ToutPanel is proprietary software (a web hosting control panel): its program, interfaces, data files, templates,
translations, documentation, installation scripts, name and logo (the "Software") are the exclusive property of its
publisher, the rights holder (the "Publisher"):

    [À COMPLÉTER par l'éditeur: legal name, legal form, registered address, registration number]

The Software is protected by intellectual property law and international treaties. It is licensed, not sold. By
installing, copying or using the Software, you (the "Licensee") accept this agreement. If you do not accept it, do not
install or use the Software.

ARTICLE 1 — RIGHT OF USE

1.1. The Publisher grants the Licensee a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable right, without the right to
     sublicense, to install and use the Software on servers under the Licensee's control, within the limits of the
     plan the Licensee holds (Article 2).
1.2. This right includes running the Software, configuring it through the means it provides (interface, command line,
     API, settings files) and making the backup copies needed to preserve it.
1.3. The Licensee may use the Software to host websites, mailboxes and services for the Licensee's own account or, if
     the plan allows it, for the Licensee's own customers, provided the Software itself is not supplied to those
     customers as a product.
1.4. The Software remains the property of the Publisher at all times. Nothing in this agreement transfers any
     intellectual property right.

ARTICLE 2 — PLANS AND LICENCE KEY

2.1. The Software is offered in several plans: free without registration (basic features), free with an account (a
     limited number of sites and selected advanced features), paid plans, and packs combining the Software with
     ToutWAF. The content, limits and prices of each plan are published and kept up to date at
     https://toutpanel.com/tarifs; they are not part of this text and may change for future versions and purchases.
2.2. Where a plan requires it, use of the relevant features is subject to a valid licence key, personal to the
     Licensee and bound to the server on which it is activated. A key is acquired under the terms of sale published at
     https://toutpanel.com.
2.3. Using a feature reserved for a plan without holding that plan, or exceeding the limits of the plan or of the key,
     is a breach of this agreement. The Software checks the licence and its limits; this check is part of the Software.

ARTICLE 3 — PROHIBITED ACTS

Except with the Publisher's prior written consent, and to the extent mandatory law provides otherwise, the Licensee
shall not:
 a) resell, rent, lend, sublicense or redistribute the Software, in whole or in part, in any form, including modified
    or embedded in another product;
 b) circumvent, disable or tamper with the licence check, the licence key, the limits of a plan or any other technical
    protection measure, or help a third party to do so;
 c) decompile, disassemble or reverse engineer the Software, in particular its licence control, or attempt to
    reconstruct its source code, except as provided by Article L.122-6-1 of the French Intellectual Property Code
    (interoperability), after having asked the Publisher for the necessary information;
 d) remove or alter the copyright, trademark or licence notices of the Software;
 e) use the Software in a manner contrary to law or to third-party rights.

ARTICLE 4 — WHAT IS ALLOWED

4.1. Expressly allowed: configuring the Software and its settings, and writing modules, plugins, themes, scripts,
     templates and integrations using the interfaces (API, hooks, module and theme formats, webhooks) that the
     Software provides for that purpose.
4.2. The Licensee owns what the Licensee writes in this way, subject to the Publisher's rights in the Software itself,
     and may distribute it freely as long as it neither contains nor redistributes any part of the Software.
4.3. Data, websites, files, databases and messages hosted with the Software belong to the Licensee (or the Licensee's
     customers); the Publisher acquires no right over them.

ARTICLE 5 — OWNERSHIP AND TRADEMARK

The Software, its code, its documentation and the "ToutPanel" mark (name and logo) remain the property of the
Publisher. No right in the mark is granted, other than the notice of origin displayed by the Software.

ARTICLE 6 — THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

The Software uses third-party components (Python libraries, interface libraries, fonts, icons) that remain subject to
their own licences, which prevail for those components. They are credited with their licence on the "Licence and
acknowledgements" page of the documentation (https://toutpanel.com/docs/legal/licence/ and
docs/content/legal/licence.md). The Software also installs or drives independent software (web server, database, PHP,
backup, mail, etc.) which it does not redistribute and which remains under its own licences.

ARTICLE 7 — UPDATES

Updates that the Publisher chooses to release are subject to this agreement unless accompanied by a separate licence.
Unless a paid plan provides otherwise, the Publisher has no obligation to provide updates or support.

ARTICLE 8 — NO WARRANTY

8.1. The Software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind other than those that the law forbids to exclude:
     in particular without warranty of absence of errors, availability, security or fitness for a particular purpose.
8.2. The Software administers servers exposed to the Internet: the Licensee is responsible for their backups, security
     and monitoring.

ARTICLE 9 — LIMITATION OF LIABILITY

9.1. Within the limits permitted by law, the Publisher is not liable for indirect damages (loss of data, business,
     revenue, customers or reputation) arising from the use of or inability to use the Software.
9.2. For a paid plan, the Publisher's total liability is limited, within the limits permitted by law, to the amounts
     paid by the Licensee for the licence during the twelve (12) months preceding the event giving rise to the claim.
9.3. Nothing in this agreement excludes or limits the Publisher's liability for wilful misconduct, gross negligence or
     personal injury, nor the rights that the law mandatorily grants to consumers.

ARTICLE 10 — TERM AND TERMINATION

10.1. The licence takes effect on installation of the Software. For a paid plan, it lasts for the term of the licence
      key and of the terms of sale.
10.2. In case of breach of this agreement (in particular of Article 3), the Publisher may terminate it after a formal
      notice left unanswered for fifteen (15) days, or without delay where the breach cannot be remedied. The
      Licensee may terminate at any time by ceasing to use the Software.
10.3. Termination never deletes the data of the Licensee or of the Licensee's customers: websites, files, databases,
      mail, backups and settings stay on the Licensee's own servers; the Publisher has no access to this data and does
      not erase it. On termination the Licensee stops using the Software (which may then be limited to basic
      features) and may export or migrate its data. Articles 3, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10.3 and 11 survive termination.

ARTICLE 11 — GENERAL

11.1. Governing law: this agreement is governed by French law. Any dispute falls within the competent French courts,
      subject to mandatory rules on jurisdiction and consumer protection.
11.2. Entire agreement: this agreement, supplemented where applicable by the terms of sale of a paid plan, is the entire
      agreement relating to the Software.
11.3. Severability: if a provision is invalid or unenforceable, the others remain in force.
11.4. Changes: the Publisher may release a revised version of this agreement with a new version of the Software; the
      applicable agreement is the one delivered with the installed version.
11.5. Contact: https://toutpanel.com/contact.php
